;; queue 522b: printf's doubles without long double. musl's fmt_fp (src/stdio/vfprintf.c) computes in long double, x87's
;; extended in software since queue 522 (about 18 us a conversion interpreted); arbace.c.run patches it to try __ci_fmt_fp first
;; when the argument is not a long double, and fmtFp64 is fmt_fp's algorithm on the double itself, step for step: the slots of
;; 10^9, the precision cut of LDBL_MANT_DIG (64) and the %a rounding of x87's 64 bits, each long double operation of fmt_fp exact
;; on a double's value but the two rounding ones, decided here as x87 decides them to nearest (round + small != round; y + 2^(63-4p)),
;; with the FE_INEXACT those two raise in crt (its conversions of a long double to an integer raise none). The bytes are musl x86_64's.

(go/func x87Double "x87Double is the double an x87 extended value (crt's Wide: the significand, then the sign and the exponent)\nholds, ok false when it holds none exactly (a long double's own value).\n" [^{:tag crt/Wide} w] :results [float64 bool]
